{
 "name": "wawel_cathedral",
 "description": "Wawel Cathedral, Krakow, at night: grey-stone Gothic nave with buttresses and warm yellow lit lancet windows under a green copper roof, the tall Clock Tower with its baroque green helm and spire on the far left (tallest, y -612), the Sigismund bell tower behind, and on the right the gold-domed Sigismund Chapel (top y -498) and the small dark Vasa Chapel dome. Right third stays under 500 tall. Anchor bottom-centre, ~980x612. Mid-grey stone so it reads on a night sky.",
